3411 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Cezar Mocan is an artist and computer programmer\056 Through the use of narrative generative systems\054 he creates simulations that reveal machine observation as a form of worldmaking\054 while investigating technological lifecycles from hype through adoption\054 infrastructuralization and obsolescence\056 He is interested in the built infrastructures which enable our digital lives\054 as well as the ways in which their presence in the natural landscape affects our perception\056 Drawing on media archaeology and art history\054 his research process traces the origins of our current thought patterns around \050technological\051 progress\056\nHis work has been exhibited in shows and screenings at SOLO Contemporary\054 Yale University\054 Center for Contemporary Art Gdansk\054 Science Gallery London\054 MEET Digital Culture Center\054 Onassis ONX Studio\054 University of Maryland\054 Inter\057Access Toronto\054 Athens Digital Art Festival\054 OFFICE IMPART\054 Panke Gallery\054 Artemis Gallery\056 His real\055time simulation work\054 Arcadia Inc\056 was recognized as a 2021 winner of the Lumen Prize in Art and Technology\056 In 2025 he was awarded the ABS Emerging Artist of the Year award and the SOLO AI Award\056 He holds a B\056S\056 in Computer Science \0502016\051 from Yale University and an M\056P\056S\056 in New Media Art \0502021\051 from New York University\054 where he also served as a research resident and adjunct professor\056)
     /K [ 2 ]
     /P 3412 0 R
     /Pg 3356 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

